license: Apache-2.0
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.23644079"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-10-25"
abstract: >-
  Lean 4 / Mathlib definitions of three candidate formal statements of the Clay Millennium
  problem "Yang–Mills existence and mass gap" (Jaffe–Witten): a Wilson lattice-limit variant (A),
  an axiomatic variant with a Yang–Mills fingerprint (B), and their conjunction (AB, recommended).
  The statements are open definitions (def … : Prop); compiled guard theorems show that known
  fake models (trivial theory, free fields, U(1), decoupled products) do not satisfy them and that
  the quantifier over compact simple gauge groups is not vacuous (SU(2) is an instance). This is
  not a proof and not progress on the problem. Declared limitations: A and AB require the Wilson
  lattice route, OS reconstruction is not formalised, and the field content is partial. The Lean
  code and the texts were written by AI agents (Claude, Anthropic) under the direction of the
  author; the verifications are mechanical (see the README).
keywords:
  - Yang–Mills
  - mass gap
  - Millennium Prize Problems
  - Lean 4
